      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sumner%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town of Sumner grew along the route of the St. Louis-San Francisco Railway.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sumner%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "At its peak, Sumner featured a bank, two churches, a school, a grain elevator, and a train stop.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sumner%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The only significant buildings still in use today in Sumner are the school and the Baptist and Christian churches.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
